<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mokvi Cathedral</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mokvi Cathedral is a medieval church in the Ochamchire district of Abkhazia, built in the 950s or 960s by Leon III, king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abkhaz-people">Abkhazians</a>, as the seat of a bishopric. A large cross-domed building, it was also a centre of learning, where the illuminated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> known as the Mokvi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gospels">Gospels</a> was copied in 1300.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mokvi-cathedral.jpg" alt="Mokvi Cathedral" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: kolhida.ru · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mokva_cathedral.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
